SQLAlchemy with Python

📌 Introduction

SQLAlchemy is a Python library used to interact with relational databases. It provides tools for executing SQL queries and working with database tables through Python objects.

SQLAlchemy supports databases such as SQLite, PostgreSQL, and MySQL.

🎯 Project Objectives

Learn the basics of SQLAlchemy.

Connect Python applications to databases.

Create and manage database tables.

Insert, retrieve, update, and delete records.

Understand Object Relational Mapping (ORM).

🛠️ Technologies Used

Python: The main programming language.

SQLAlchemy: A Python SQL toolkit and Object Relational Mapper (ORM).

SQLite: A lightweight relational database.

✨ Features

Database connection management.

Table creation using Python classes.

Data insertion and retrieval.

Updating and deleting records.

Working with database relationships.

Supporting multiple database systems.

📦 Installation

Install SQLAlchemy using pip:

pip install sqlalchemy 

💻 Example Code

The following example demonstrates how to create a database table and insert and retrieve data using SQLAlchemy.

from sqlalchemy import create_engine, String from sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase from sqlalchemy.orm import Mapped, mapped_column from sqlalchemy.orm import Session # Create a database connection engine = create_engine("sqlite:///users.db") # Define the base class class Base(DeclarativeBase): pass # Define the User model class User(Base): tablename = "users" id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True) name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(50)) # Create the database table Base.metadata.create_all(engine) # Insert and retrieve data with Session(engine) as session: user = User(name="Ali") session.add(user) session.commit() users = session.query(User).all() for user in users: print(user.id, user.name) 

🚀 How to Run

Install Python.

Install SQLAlchemy.

Create a Python file named main.py.

Copy the example code into the file.

Run the application:

python main.py 

A database file named users.db will be created automatically.

📚 Important Concepts

Engine: Manages communication between Python and the database.

Model: A Python class representing a database table.

ORM: Allows developers to work with database records as Python objects.

Session: Manages database operations and transactions.

Primary Key: Uniquely identifies each record.

Query: Retrieves data from a database.

📖 CRUD Operations

CRUD represents the four basic database operations.

OperationDescriptionCreateInsert new recordsReadRetrieve recordsUpdateModify existing recordsDeleteRemove records 

